1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,689
Eighty-three dollars at 8 p.m.

2
00:00:02,709 --> 00:00:05,882
One hundred and eleven and a half at noon.

3
00:00:05,902 --> 00:00:07,621
Ninety-seven at the close.

4
00:00:07,641 --> 00:00:17,242
In a single day, a company that didn't
exist six years ago became worth more on

5
00:00:17,262 --> 00:00:20,530
the stock market than Meta.

6
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:29,608
On Thursday, November 19, Anthropic, the
company behind the Claude assistant,

7
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:34,796
listed on the Nasdaq under the ticker
A-N-T.

8
00:00:34,816 --> 00:00:39,341
The IPO price had been set the night
before at 83 dollars, above the expected

9
00:00:39,361 --> 00:00:40,404
range of 70 to 78.

10
00:00:40,424 --> 00:00:46,307
At the open, 11:48 New York time, the
stock jumped to 111 dollars 50: up 34

11
00:00:46,327 --> 00:00:46,936
percent.

12
00:00:46,956 --> 00:00:48,357
Then the session cooled.

13
00:00:48,377 --> 00:00:53,055
It closed at 97 dollars 17, up 17 percent
from the IPO price.

14
00:00:53,075 --> 00:00:57,933
More than 846 million shares changed
hands, more than SpaceX on its first day

15
00:00:57,953 --> 00:00:58,440
in June.

16
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:03,735
According to Forbes, the offering raised
81 billion dollars.

17
00:01:03,755 --> 00:01:05,281
Bloomberg calls it a record IPO.

18
00:01:05,301 --> 00:01:11,001
The valuation depends on how you count:
1.27 trillion dollars on shares

19
00:01:11,021 --> 00:01:15,914
outstanding; close to 1.77 trillion on a
fully diluted basis.

20
00:01:15,934 --> 00:01:23,710
Either way, that is more than Meta, valued
at 1.55 trillion.

21
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:26,116
The timing is no accident.

22
00:01:26,136 --> 00:01:30,770
For three weeks, the AI sector has been
shaken: Nvidia's stock has lost about 20

23
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:33,562
percent and its CEO, Jensen Huang, has
resigned.

24
00:01:33,582 --> 00:01:36,386
Investors were asking whether the AI
bubble was about to deflate.

25
00:01:36,406 --> 00:01:40,210
Anthropic chose this moment to test their
appetite.

26
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:53,500
The result: a strong start, but a close 13
percent below the day's high.

27
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,708
Scenario one: confidence returns.

28
00:01:56,728 --> 00:02:03,305
The stock settles above its IPO price and
lifts chip suppliers across Asia.

29
00:02:03,325 --> 00:02:05,780
Scenario two: volatility continues.

30
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:10,172
Retail investors, very active on day one,
take their profits.

31
00:02:10,192 --> 00:02:13,603
Scenario three: the domino effect.

32
00:02:13,623 --> 00:02:19,130
Other AI players speed up their own
listings to catch the window.

33
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:26,857
One thing is certain: for the first time,
a pure AI company is publicly traded.

34
00:02:26,877 --> 00:02:36,611
Every trading day is now a real-time poll
on the future of artificial intelligence.

35
00:02:36,631 --> 00:02:37,384
TempoBrief.

36
00:02:37,404 --> 00:02:39,400
The news that matters, in minutes.
